**Full-width layout.** I removed the two width caps — `main { max-width: 1040px }` and the desktop `max-width: 1140px` — so the page now fills the window at every size and the two columns grow with it. Measured: the content box is 1349 px at a 1366 window, 1872 px at 1920 and 2511 px at 2560, with no horizontal scroll at any width; phones are unaffected because the content was already wider than the screen there.

| Window | Left column (board) | Right column | Columns end |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 2560 | 1436 wide, board 1415 × 663 | incline y 73, hanger y 323, model y 627 (1061 wide) | 96 px apart |
| 1920 | 1068 wide, board 1047 × 497 | 790 wide, model y 645 | 96 px apart |
| 1366 | 749 wide, board 728 × 345 | 554 wide, model y 663 | 16 px apart |
| 1024 | 553 wide, board 532 | 409 wide, model y 699 | 27 px apart |
| 390 | full width, sticky board, single column | stacked, 12 px gaps | — |

The board keeps its 1000 × 640 proportions, so on a big monitor it is now genuinely large — about 660 px tall at 2560 wide. Two things you may want a second look at, since they are the honest consequence of filling the window: the **Release the cart** button stretches to the width of the run bar (899 px at 1920, 1267 px at 2560), and the record-sheet table and analysis rows spread across the full width. Say the word if you'd rather the run bar and those two cards kept a readable cap while the rig still filled the screen.

**Force arrows off by default.** The switch in **Model & timing** now starts off, and the arrows stay hidden until you turn it on. I changed the state default and the switch's initial `aria-checked`, and I also handled the storage side: the saved payload version went from `v: 1` to `v: 2`, and loading only honours a saved `showForces` from a v2 save. Without that, anyone who had already opened the app would have kept loading the old arrows-on value and seen no change at all. Verified all three paths in the browser: a fresh visit with no saved state shows the switch off and the arrow group `display: none`; a v1 save flips to off on load and is rewritten as v2; and once you turn the arrows on yourself that choice survives a reload (checked `inline` after reload with `showForces: true` stored, then off again).

I also confirmed a normal run still works after the change — **Release the cart** recorded `t = 0.785 s` into Mass 1, it round-tripped through storage under `v: 2` and came back after a reload, and the analysis recomputed (`t_avg = 0.785 s · W = 1.225 J · P = 1.561 W`). No console errors at any width. I cleared that test trial afterwards, so the saved state is clean, and I left the arrows off. [README.md](work-power/README.md) was updated for both changes. Nothing is committed.
