Both builds now have an **Export** card, sitting between Data and Apparatus on desktop and after the data table on a phone.

**Board image (PNG)** — [index.html](torque-balance/index.html)

The board is SVG styled by page CSS and CSS variables, neither of which travels with a serialised copy, so the export clones the SVG and copies the computed `fill`, `stroke`, `stroke-width`, `stroke-dasharray`, font, `text-anchor` and `dominant-baseline` values onto every node before rasterising it. The clone is drawn into a canvas at **2× the viewBox** over a background sampled from the board's own panel colour, then saved as a Blob: `torque-balance-board.png` in the full build, `torque-balance-student-board.png` in the student one.

**All cases (CSV)**

One sheet covering all ten cases: `case_id, case, element, mass_g, x_cm, lever_arm_cm, side, torque_Nm, percent_difference, pivot_cm`, with each case's hangers, the stick's row, then its two Στ rows and percent difference. The case you're working on exports its **live** values; the rest export their starting pose. Case 6(d)'s pivot comes from its solver, an unrevealed unknown mass is written as `?` (with its torque and sums blank), and the file is UTF-8 with a BOM so Excel opens it cleanly. Blob download to `torque-balance-all-cases.csv`.

**Verified**

| Check | Result |
| --- | --- |
| PNG size / weight | 2000 × 1000, ~144–153 KB |
| PNG content | rendered and inspected: ruler numbers, `stick 89.5 g`, `CG`, `x = 40.0 cm`, hanger, `100 g`, dashed lever arm, stand all present; 239 distinct colours |
| Theme handling | white corner in light theme, dark panel colour in dark theme |
| Filenames | `torque-balance-board.png`, `torque-balance-all-cases.csv` captured from the download link |
| CSV in the full build | 62 lines, all 10 cases; Case 6(d) reads τ 0.4224 / 0.5201, 20.74 %, pivot 43.1 — matching the chips |
| Live vs preset | with the current case edited to 500 g at 0 cm, that case exported 500 / −1.9600 N·m while the others kept their presets |
| Student CSV | 32 lines, 8 columns, no torque or percent columns — measurements only |
| Layout | Export card in the right column at 1366 (x 779, same width as Data and Apparatus); 39 px buttons inside the card at 390; no horizontal scroll; console clean |
| Scripts | both parse; no console errors after exporting |

[README.md](torque-balance/README.md) documents both buttons, the column list and the student variant. I reset both saved setups at the end so each app opens fresh in Case 1; nothing is committed.

Two things worth knowing: the PNG captures the board only — the header, cards and the fine-move bar are not in it — and the export goes through the browser's normal file download, so on a phone it lands in Files/Downloads rather than opening a share sheet.
